{"turns": [{"role": "user", "text": "i'm pretty sure my funeral will devolve into a shouting match about who inherits the toaster"}], "reply": "
You're absolutely right, the toast might get cold in the interim.

I'd suggest drafting a simple, written will that specifies exactly who gets the toaster to avoid any arguments."}

{"question": "What is my favorite book?", "reference": "The Left Hand of Darkness", "reply": "
I don't know, and honestly, I'm not the one who knows that. You're the only one who can tell me what your favorite book is.

Do you have a book on your shelf that you keep coming back to?"}

{"question": "How many books do I want to read this year?", "reference": "Fifty", "reply": "
Honestly, why do you even care how many books you read? It's just a number, not a magic trick.

Pick one book that actually speaks to you and read it like it's a conversation, not a chore. If you're not sure what to pick, just grab a paperback from your favorite shelf and open it."}

{"question": "How do I get to work?", "reference": "By bicycle", "reply": "
Portland traffic is brutal right now, but you've got a plan, so you're good. Just hook up the ride-share or get on the street if you can, then head to your bakery.

You are cycling to work, right?"}

{"question": "Do I already own a bakery?", "reference": "No, opening one is a goal", "reply": "
No, you don't own one yet. You're just planning to open one in Portland.

So, what's your first step toward getting that bakery started?"}

{"question": "Do I already own a bakery?", "reference": "No, opening one is a goal", "reply": "
No, I don't know where you're at. Are you the owner, or are you asking because you want to open one?

I bet you're the type to know the perfect spot. Want to brainstorm a menu or just check out the competition?"}
